{"title":"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Official_MAA)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Official MAA)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(writing_equations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (writing equations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_without_words\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution without words</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b3a42d2996b0877ff90e40516ca63d24be8310a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lies strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2caa0918e410a55dfb04ac612c1f569e7e1dcbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb16ce1bc134fc7f40839c34a43a6f334ff8ad4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=ED=DB=BC.$\" width=\"192\" height=\"13\" /> The degree measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c80f7cbc6e8017ab735d473c6f3eb2e66a40511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e27ce12b66c38e61f3aeeeec6ac0760eebc7e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); pair A, B, C, D, F; A = (0, tan(3 * pi / 7)); B = (1, 0); C = (-1, 0); F = rotate(90/7, A) * (A - (0, 2)); D = rotate(900/7, F) * A;  draw(A -- B -- C -- cycle); draw(F -- D); draw(D -- B);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, W); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, F, E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"475\" />\n</p><p>If we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2c830e136e667485791216de260e10db2c2195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we can find all other angles through these two properties:\n1. Angles in a triangle sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />.\n2. The base angles of an isosceles triangle are congruent.\n</p><p>Now we angle chase. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f5fa270ea8eb1730d1fe0a50fee89ae734da84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADE}=\\angle{EAD}=x$\" width=\"171\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54156405bf71b515a4bfbe2fb526511a2da31e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AED} = 180-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"149\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ceb226b4645c2c67d526ffab5152a137f5496b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BED}=\\angle{EBD}=2x$\" width=\"182\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dc843473d5d408d5af7b4f0315da5e63133822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EDB} = 180-4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc0dec5633c5c69e40a624ff68e0a5cb58262c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BDC} = \\angle{BCD} = 3x$\" width=\"182\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2add66ccd51029a62a4191086aae03951b56d444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBD} = 180-6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> as given by the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/7/867290e123c69d3d567594d470ce7d7d663e92f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABC} = \\angle{ACB}$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d7975348704465b87f29d0b3cae4e1e02deb0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180-4x=3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b772310d8448f5a5effb665461c372a34da2df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180/7^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, and our desired angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8994eb36574f1458d2ee3824b34658f345eabc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[180-4\\left(\\frac{180}{7}\\right) = \\frac{540}{7}\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"43\" /> for an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e700a60eb682c433db59300195552dfd7b4a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>See here for a video solution: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4e8Hk04Ax_E\">https://youtu.be/4e8Hk04Ax_E</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2c830e136e667485791216de260e10db2c2195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in degrees. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c15ae3b4e5ad0d84f0edf63632dd5e35a1b627c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADE}=x$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />.\nBy Exterior Angle Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c610b5935928e7a2b822af15479336a7e1276b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BED}=2x$\" width=\"101\" height=\"12\" />.\nBy Exterior Angle Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/8810a26f59e2c67b5f2ff052a7e2a294fef0a03e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/0313baf24420bc2d8b3b0b6ec3b30e90f7e6146f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BDC}=3x$\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" />.\nThis tells us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e8a2c7a37280a70ff06efb33116fe4c0a79e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BCA}=\\angle{ABC}=3x$\" width=\"178\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb7316c6854d0e83a36b21e2897950d67d5ac31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+3x+x=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />.\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed6814334dcd737468becd963d913eabab93f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{180}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> and we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9be069f25a2fc6c472263754046ac2140b632e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABC}=3x=\\frac{540}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"153\" height=\"37\" /> to get an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e700a60eb682c433db59300195552dfd7b4a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Official_MAA.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Official_MAA)\">Solution 3 (Official MAA)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Official MAA)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/823c8bea1e9b183b1cd8fa4cc451c092cb24c74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\angle ABC = \\angle ACB$\" width=\"169\" height=\"13\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d78a64836eee0705b202e1ac116dee8ce03a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBD = 180^\\circ - 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/629bfe7c966d095fd79948681f137725b9cdf538.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle DBE = x - \\angle CBD = x - (180^\\circ - 2x) =  3x - 180^\\circ\\!.\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"18\" />Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b2778f025e98fe4c78a1385c78f83edbf307fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EDA$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/77500eaad809c17abfb6f78eeff713aa02d7e61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are also isosceles,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f1b072cce901fe5d608b716ff88da0361ae9d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAC =\\frac12(\\angle EAD + \\angle ADE) = \\frac12(\\angle BED)= \\frac12(\\angle DBE)\\]\" width=\"458\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a130bf3ee0d36bc626218a59913d6d47dcfcf24f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac12 (3x - 180^\\circ) = \\frac32x-90^\\circ\\!.\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba61b3232c79c2589025c0476f31db40a3eaa65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d803f67d33430e0718f1d9b196d165057bb2915c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac32x - 90^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"172\" height=\"37\" />, and it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a909fc0f2ff7df866c313604542a7153b941768d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = x = \\left(\\frac{540}7\\right)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"181\" height=\"46\" />. The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed02a4751c34d2ad73a90b8dc59b5bd7062e2130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540+7 = 547$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800a1b87e83f02303a544a1cc3b37b3a774d9483.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E; real a = 180/7;  A = (0,0); B = dir(180 - a/2); C = dir(180 + a/2); D = extension(B, B + dir(270 + a), A, C); E = extension(D, D + dir(90 - 2*a), A, B);  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(B--D--E);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(0)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, N); [/asy]\" width=\"232\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25</a>\n(Almost Mirrored)\n</p><p>See here for a video solution:\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4XkA0DwuqYk\">https://youtu.be/4XkA0DwuqYk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28writing_equations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(writing_equations)\">Solution 4 (writing equations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (writing equations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>graph soon\n</p><p>We write equations based on the triangle sum of angles theorem. There are angles that do not need variables as the less variables the better.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b84a73516b426c175b59602544f1e0b8e8f1def.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\angle A &amp;= y \\\\ \\angle B &amp;= x+z \\\\ \\angle C &amp;= \\frac{180-x}{2} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"113\" height=\"87\" />\n</p><p>Then, using triangle sum of angles theorem, we find that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be6c732cf1f64c4d91f9a9bfce0cfc16d7bc8d5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C = x+y+z+\\frac{180-x}{2}=180 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"359\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now we just need to find the variables.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4cf2208b3b44836a7454263620bf533f485714.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (180-2y)+z = 180&amp; \\\\ (180-2z)+y+\\frac{180-x}{2} = 180&amp; \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"249\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p>Notice how all the equations equal 180. We can use this to write\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f34b18a832fd3a9a4293586444564235857fc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (180-2y)+z = (180-2z)+y+\\frac{180-x}{2}=x+y+z+\\frac{180-x}{2} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"518\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfece596b66c068e4c76cd9674991ab58999a953.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (180-2y)+z=(180-2z)+y+\\frac{180-x}{2} \\\\ 360-4y+2z=360-4z+2y+180-x \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"336\" height=\"61\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d731752252d417219c0a017d612e3387dfe359b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6z=6y+180-x \\\\ x=6y-6z+180 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"142\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d52cf234223c5632b0fe62cce6ad27f9ba7127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (180-2y)+z=6y-6z+180+y+z+\\frac{180-(6y-6+180)}{2} \\\\ 360-4y+2z=12y-12z+360+2y+2z+180-6y+6z-180 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"520\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca8f33ad88cbdb7f90921c2e906bcb1f0b75eb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6z=12y&amp; \\\\ z=2y&amp; \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"69\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Theres more. We are at a dead end right now because we forgot that the problem states that the triangle is isosceles. With this, we can write the equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cccb5edf3cf0246ee4bb3a3cb5c17bda75abf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{180-x}{2}=x+z \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cab3f0704de3232f601b03d02a45d46103c172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac3b8f2363785ccd08274c3745a17bd776c8a7d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{180-x}{2}=x+2y \\\\ 180-x=2x+4y \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"142\" height=\"61\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac0372482e51489de1960c8a2d42ef105d9db98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 180-(6y-6z+180)=2(6y-6z+180)+4y&amp; \\\\ 180-6y+12y-180=12y-24y+360+4y&amp; \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"367\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf91c2389369dbd2c8905954613f85e69ae0968.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6y=-8y+360&amp; \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>With this, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cba04def07737e6ea80d37e8e00557db1e0e52c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} y=\\frac{180}{7} \\\\ x=\\frac{180}{7} \\\\ z=\\frac{360}{7} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"63\" height=\"123\" />\n</p><p>And a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6ab89c17b0ff2e0481bb387b4bdc3eb3f29ba2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180}{7}+\\frac{360}{7} = \\frac{540}{7} = \\boxed{547}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"205\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OrenSH&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"OrenSH (page does not exist)\">orenbad</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/O_o_-yjGrOU?t=333\">https://youtu.be/O_o_-yjGrOU?t=333</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IH7yM3L5xjA\">https://youtu.be/IH7yM3L5xjA</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mgRNqSDCvgM\">https://youtu.be/mgRNqSDCvgM</a> ~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_without_words\">Solution without words</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution without words\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_AIME_I_1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3f/2020_AIME_I_1.png/450px-2020_AIME_I_1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"439\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/3f/2020_AIME_I_1.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_AIME_I_1a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f4/2020_AIME_I_1a.png/460px-2020_AIME_I_1a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"460\" height=\"434\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f4/2020_AIME_I_1a.png/690px-2020_AIME_I_1a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/f4/2020_AIME_I_1a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I\" title=\"2020 AIME I\">2020 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-ali